;; clj-kondo settings for `make kondocheck`, which CI runs. An error here fails the
;; build, so the linters below are off because they fire on code that is correct:
;;
;;   :unresolved-symbol        names jolt's host defines, and macro-bound DSLs
;;   :unexpected-recur         recur inside jolt's own loop-shaped macros
;;   :not-a-function           the case-like macros in clojure.data.json and
;;                             clojure.pprint read as calling a character
;;   :namespace-name-mismatch  stubs that provide another library's namespace
;;
;; Every other error-level linter is enforced, and a malformed ns form is promoted
;; to one. (jolt's own ns refuses those at load; this finds them without loading.)
{:linters {:unresolved-symbol {:level :off}
           :unexpected-recur {:level :off}
           :not-a-function {:level :off}
           :namespace-name-mismatch {:level :off}
           :syntax {:level :error}
           :unknown-ns-option {:level :error}}}
